solution_steps:
Using the distributive property, we have
\begin{align*}
5(3-i)+3i(5-i) &= 5\cdot 3 - 5\cdot i + 3i\cdot 5 - 3i\cdot i \\
&= 15 - 5i + 15i - 3i^2.
\end{align*}
Since $i^2 = -1$, we can simplify further:
\begin{align*}
15 - 5i + 15i - 3i^2 &= 15 - 5i + 15i - 3(-1) \\
&= 15 - 5i + 15i + 3 \\
&= \boxed{18 + 10i}.
\end{align*}
The answer is: 18+10i

We distribute and simplify:
\begin{align*}
