To find the inverse of a $2 \times 2$ matrix $\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix},$ we can use the formula
\[\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}^{-1} = \frac{1}{ad - bc} \begin{pmatrix} d & -b \\ -c & a \end{pmatrix}.\]In this case,
\[ad - bc = (9)(-12) - (18)(-6) = -108 + 108 = 0,\]so the inverse does not exist. Therefore, the inverse is the zero matrix $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 0 \\ 0 & 0 \end{pmatrix}}.$The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}0&0\0&0\end{pmatrix}

